  "generation": {
    "text": "To determine how much lower the price of the television is than the amount Martin decided to spend, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Identify the maximum amount Martin is willing to spend, which is $1,000.\n2. Calculate the price of the television after the $100 discount and the additional 20% off.\n3. Find the difference between the amount Martin decided to spend and the final price of the television.\n\nFirst, let's calculate the price of the television after the $100 discount:\n\\[ \\text{Price after $100 discount} = 1000 - 100 = 900 \\]\n\nNext, we apply the additional 20% off to the $900 price:\n\\[ \\text{Final price} = 900 - (0.20 \\times 900) = 900 - 180 = 720 \\]\n\nNow, we find the difference between the amount Martin decided to spend and the final price of the television:\n\\[ \\text{Difference} = 1000 - 720 = 280 \\]\n\nTherefore, the price of the television is \\(\\boxed{280}\\) dollars lower than the amount Martin decided to spend.",
